4 The SPSE Problem
In the previous section we introduced the SPICES algorithm and discussed how it retrieves single-
particle energies in a purely free system. However, motivated by the physics of interacting systems,
we would like for SPICES to be able to solve the more general problem wherein the free model is
embedded in a larger system that may not be globally free.
Here we formalize the general problem of estimating free spectra of a free Hamiltonian embedded
in an interacting system.
