7 Robustness to perturbation
We now verify the contour conditions of Theorem 13 for Hamiltonians with interactions outside
a preferred energy band, while keeping the single-particle energies inside that band intact. The
perturbed Hamiltonian may contain arbitrary number-conserving interactions on modes outside the
target window, provided those interactions do not couple the inside and outside mode algebras (as
defined by the unperturbed Hamiltonian).
