8.7 Proof of the main hardness theorem
Proof of Theorem 42.GivenU,g , outputM = 2m + 4, the Pauli list(84), the symbolic operator
N =WN stdW† withW from (107), and the compiler established in Section 8.6. All these descriptions
are constructed deterministically in polynomial time without deciding the trace-sign branch. We
verify the five claims.
1. Expandingn j = (I+Z j)/2forj=R,Sgives exactlyH= 8I+ 8Z R + (17/2)ZS.
2. Thefactorsof W areunitary, soconjugationpreservestheeigenvaluesandbinomialmultiplicities
ofN std. The commutation relation[H,N] = 0follows from Lemma 49.
50
3. The same lemma gives the stated tensor decompositions, withV+ = 2Λ S−I and V− =
(32/17)ΛR−I, each of norm one and conserving spectator occupation. This is precisely the
model of Section 7.1, taking all free spectator energies to be zero andλ= 17/2.
4. The tensor decompositions identifyE⋆ = 16in the positive branch andE⋆ = 17in the negative
branch. All free spectator energies are zero, so this is the unique protected energy in[15, 18],
the endpoint gap is∆Ω = 1, and|λ|= 17/2<16.
5. Corollary 59 and Lemma 60 supply all three primitives to error2−r, with resources polynomial
in|U|,m,g −1,r,ℓ qry for number measurement and joint evolution, and additionally ineβ for
Gibbs preparation. Sinceg−1 is polynomially bounded inm, these meet Definition 10. At
β = log(3M), we haveeβ = 3M, so preparation also has polynomial cost. In particular, setting
r=M 2 preserves polynomial size at this temperature.
This proves all claimed properties of the reduction.
