B The LP estimator
Letρ be an unknown probability measure on the unit torus, with Fourier coefficientsuℓ, and suppose
that only noisy coefficientsbuℓ with|ℓ|≤T are available. Our argument rests on the one-dimensional
stability theorem of Chen–De–Huang–Nadimpalli–Servedio–Yang [37], which we use without proof.
Here T = [0, 1)is the unit torus with its toroidal metric,W T
1 is the Wasserstein-1 distance for that
metric, and the Fourier coefficients of a probability measureρonTareuℓ =
R
T e2πiℓx dρ(x),ℓ∈Z.
Lemma 63(Stability of low-frequency Fourier data [37, Theorem 7, cased = 1]).Let0 <ε′< 1
2,
and set
T=
 6
