), a possible explanation for the non-monotonic error degradation observed in the pressure field is the influence of floating-point round-off effects and catastrophic cancellation inherent to 
1
/
ε
1/\varepsilon
 predictor scalings, though establishing this definitively would require further precision tests. In the kinetic regime (
