Finally, while we focused on adiabatic perturbations, the peaked axion field fluctuations can also source isocurvature perturbations. In particular, when axion dark matter is produced by the (kinetic) misalignment mechanism, or when baryon asymmetry is generated by axiogenesis, the axion field perturbations source dark matter or baryon isocurvature perturbations that inherit the peaked spectrum. Such peaked isocurvature perturbations could serve as a distinctive target for future galaxy surveys.








