would require matrix-valued analogues of the dynamic sampling and
cumulative-feedback ideas used for LPs, together with a way to control
matrix-response and constraint-feedback errors over the entire trajectory.
Our classical analysis suggests that online-learning and martingale
techniques may provide a useful starting point for this direction.






