We leave a thorough investigation of these problems for future work.






Note added.
—During the final stage of writing this manuscript, we became aware of an independent work by Tirone et al. 
[
57
]
, where they also showed the universal achievability of distillable entanglement by a different technique.
The main difference lies in the way of ensuring robust distillation after state tomography.
We achieve this by employing state merging for compound sources, while they do so by running a hashing protocol on the output isotropic states with an unknown parameter.






