.","Discussion




We have established a transport theory for shaped waves in disordered media, in which the transported quantity is an involutive matrix rather than a scalar radiance.
In lossless media, the nonlinear MTE yields analytical predictions for transmission eigenchannels, including the sinusoidal intensity profile of open channels and 
cosh
\cosh
-shaped evanescence of closed channels, and reveals their geometric origin.
It also clarifies the relation to previous interpretations of the open-channel profile based on a return probability 
22
, 
24
, 
25
