 remain close to zero. Across all three clusters and all tested regularization weights, these results indicate comparable predictive accuracy and provide no evidence that the SL data prefer models with fitted halo offsets.
The total mass distributions remain broadly similar, although the magnitudes of the fitted halo offsets vary with regularization. These findings illustrate the non-uniqueness of the mass decomposition between the regularized grid and cluster-scale halo profiles. Given this dependence on the mass decomposition, there are limitations to inferences about cluster dynamics or DM physics based on fitted offsets.






In addition, we evaluate the effects of halo positional freedom and regularization on magnification and time-delay predictions. For the full sample, the median maximum fixed-free differences across the tested regularization weights remain below 
