We have shown in detail that cosmologically coupled phenomenology with flexible 
κ
\kappa
 can exist in linearized GR.
We emphasize that the existence of a viable linearized GR model does not establish that cosmological coupling must occur.
As with any GR solution, data will determine which scenarios “on paper” are most appropriate for describing nature.
Although we have used the SVT machinery often employed in PT to guarantee that only scalar DOFs are present and well-defined, 
