Conclusions




In this paper, we have studied the consequences of causality for the dynamical response coefficients in the point-particle effective theory, at leading order in the gradient expansion. We showed that, under the assumptions of positivity (i.e., absorptivity of the system; see Eq. (
3.5
)) and suitable high-frequency convergence of the Green’s function, classical retardedness of the response implies a series of inequalities among the Wilson coefficients of the EFT. In the absence of dissipation, the first few bounds take the form (
5.1
).






Despite the analogy with the positive moment problem for scattering amplitudes in unitary and causal quantum field theories in Minkowski space 
[
10
]
