B_{3}
 provides a way to quantify the validity of the single-mode approximation.






Second, for more compact stars, where the renormalization-group running of the Love numbers becomes non-negligible, the bounds become strongly sensitive to the renormalization scale and are generally violated as this scale is lowered or increased. This confirms an expectation already suggested by the black-hole example: the bounds (
5.1
) need not hold once strong-gravity effects become important. A more detailed analysis of the assumptions underlying the bounds (
5.1
), and of their validity in the strong-gravity regime, is presented in a companion work 
[
37
]
.






We note that, although 
