. This suggests the possibility of deriving bounds involving both the gravito-electric and gravito-magnetic Love numbers of a compact object. Such an analysis would require going beyond the worldline description and spatially resolving the object.
Another interesting direction would be to constrain or rule out specific families of equations of state. At present, our bounds are not strong enough to rule out equations of state that exhibit explicit pathologies (e.g., superluminality), such as the polytrope with 
