here is a consequence of the self-duality of the square lattice,
rather than a generic feature of the dynamics. If so, other 2D
lattices with different geometries may exhibit two distinct
percolation transitions, with an intermediate phase characterized
either by the coexistence of positive and negative percolating
clusters, as in three dimensions, or by their absence.
