4.4 
Biases in Sample Selection and Fitting Methodology




Any empirical scaling relation is susceptible to biases introduced by the sample selection function and the statistical methodology used to derive it. In the context of the IRX relation, these biases can artificially inflate the perceived scatter and shift the best-fit parameters. Our analysis identifies and quantifies several such biases.






Sample Selection and Observational Limits:
 The construction of a multi-wavelength SFG sample, as used here and in 
76
, imposes implicit limits on the range of observable attenuation. UV-selected samples are inherently biased against heavily obscured, edge-on systems where the UV flux may fall below the detection threshold. Our examination of GALEX survey depth in Figure 
3
