1 
Conventions




Fourier transform - Wikipedia
 has a nice table summarizing (non-)unitary and ordinary/angular frequency definition.






The unitary, ordinary frequency definition is the simplest, and most commonly used in Mathematics.






In Quantum mechanics, angular frequency with the non-unitary definition is used. The reason for angular frequency is probably for the canonical momentum relationship.






In 
Fourier transform definition conventions and formulas
, John Cook unifies all different conventions in a parameterized definition, which can have 8 combinations. Mathematica has a different parametrization in 
FourierTransform—Wolfram Language Documentation
. He pointed out the relationship between the 2 parameterization in 
Fourier transforms and conventions in Mathematica
.








