Chapter 45 
Changelog of null-tests performed in POLARBEAR large-patch analysis




Below is the changelog of all null-test runs performed in the POLARBEAR analysis in 
part
 
5
.
They are reproduced here for reference.






Note:








•




Semantic versioning is used: 
major.minor.bugfix
. Major versions all share the same map-making, for example v0.6 through v0.6.6. Minor versions differ in post-mapmaking, for example how they are grouped to coadd, how the spectra are generated, etc.




•




Since v0.13.2.1: revert to plotting 
C
l
C_{l}
 instead.




•




Since v0.6.2, 
C
l
​
B
l
2
C_{l}B_{l}^{2}
 is plotted instead.




•




Since v0.2.1, the spectra is plot 
without
 the dof factor of 
l
⁡
(
l
+
1
)
2
​
π
\frac{l(l+1)}{2\pi}
. i.e. the previous spectra are so called 
D
l
D_{l}
.




•




If you see 
a + bj
, interpret 
a
 as the value and 
b
 as the error-bar. It is just a shortcut to represent elements of 
ℝ
2
\mathbb{R}^{2}
 as elements of 
ℂ
\mathbb{C}
.




•




Changelog:




•




v1.0.2
: The only bug fix is the patch that fix ground template mentioned below:








–




Dominic found that tweaking how AnalysisBackend construct the ground template can remove the stripes. I applied a patch at AnalysisBackend commit 07b6610. Merge to cleanup?




–




What the patch does:








*




before the patch, a point-source masked TOD is used to construct the ground template




*




with the patch, TOD without point-source mask is used to construct the ground template












•




v1.1.1: (superseded by fix in v1.0.2) Only real-mapmaking for deugging strips in I-maps: change group template from 0.5 to 1.




•




v1.1: (superseded by fix in v1.0.2) Only real-mapmaking for deugging strips in I-maps: change group template from 0.24 to 0.5.




•




v1.0.1
: add 
--deconvolve
 to real mapmaking, everything else identical. i.e. sign-flip-noise from real map is not regenerated.




•




v1.0.0
: identical to v1.0.0-beta except no. of TTEEBB simulation increased from 358 to 512.




•




v1.0.0-beta
:








–




updated theory spectra input using Planck 2018 values and CLASS.




–




point source mask:








*




boolean mask in mapmaking changed to 3.5 arcmin (from default 5 arcmin)




*




map to pseudo-spectra mask changed to Gaussian (from 
C
∞
C^{\infty}
 taper with inner and outer radius) for mode-coupling niceness, with FWHM at 10.5 arcmin.








–




removed null tests that involve random splits, reducing from 24 to 21 null tests.




–




128 TTEE, TTBB simulations; 512 TTEEBB simulations with 358 only included in this report.








•




v0.13.4
:








–




zero-padding on maps changed from 1.3x to 2x




–




“naïve” Wiener filter on temperature weights removed








•




v0.13.3
: use sign-flip noise in TT/EE/BB/noise simulations




•




v0.13.2.1
: null-spectra plotting changing from 
C
l
​
B
l
2
C_{l}B_{l}^{2}
 to 
C
l
C_{l}




•




v0.13.2: Fixed a bug that causes v0.13.1 wrong. i.e. this one has the correct output from 
--correct_poleff




•




v0.13.1: 
--correct_poleff
 is appleid to real map to correct for the polarization efficiency which effectively rescale the TOD.




•




v0.13:








–




add point sources: 
fixed_sources_pccsinlp
 from 
pointing/sources.py




–




OLEA projection




–




completely new pipeline for post-mapmaking








*




no intermediate binning, only 1 single binning step is used in the final step




*




mode-coupling:








·




bug fixed




·




with and without point-source mask are compared








*




pseudo-spectra:








·




fully implement 
no_diag
 variant for every case (also the cross cases has been unified to avoid bugs)




·




should be numerically more stable (due to how the old one binning things)








*




new filter transfer function definition: 
C
~
l
=
∑
ℓ
′
F
ℓ
​
M
ℓ
​
ℓ
′
​
B
ℓ
′
2
​
C
ℓ
′
\widetilde{C}_{l}=\sum_{\ell^{\prime}}F_{\ell}M_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}B_{\ell^{\prime}}^{2}C_{\ell^{\prime}}




*




there’s only 1 single mask (per temperature/polarization, i.e. the final mask) used across all observations (“10”-day cycles). Previously, each observation has their own mask, where as the mode-coupling matrices are calculated once using the final mask, which is what’s done in the low-
ℓ
\ell
 pipeline. But since the low-
ℓ
\ell
 pipeline calculated the mode-coupling by simulation rather than analytical like the high-
ℓ
\ell
 pipeline, this shouldn’t be a problem for low-
ℓ
\ell
.




*




post mapmaking was more expensive than mapmaking, and it is now much cheaper. Debug QoS can almost accommodate the whole post-mapmaking calculation.








–




binning is done slightly differently in null-spectra








•




v0.12:








–




use 1 arcmin.




–




pseudo-spectra pipeline requires more memory than Cori I has available per node. So only maps are produced but no spectra.








•




v0.11:








–




largepatch4 datasets




–




merged 
AnalysisBackend/cleanup/4254c87
 to the high-l post-making pipelines




–




