Quantum dense network coding is an emerging area of research that has promising applications in cryptography and network communications.
We generalize quantum dense network coding to 
n
n
-sender MNs, introducing in Protocol 
III.2
 a family of multiparty affine transformations that require half as many qudits of communication to evaluate as dits.
We prove that a strict separation exists between the success probability of evaluating the multiparty affine transformation between 
