IV.2
, we exploit these characteristics to develop a procedure for robust SDI estimation of the effective visibility of graph states and measurements in entanglement-assisted quantum MNs.






From a physical perspective, quantum dense network coding with graph states presents a fascinating scenario in which entanglement-assisted quantum MNs drastically outperform other resource configurations under strict communication constraints.
The strong communication advantages and noise robustness result from the bound on 
