Contact binaries are generally expected to have low Rossby numbers owing to their short orbital periods and synchronous rotation.
Observationally, they tend to occupy a lower-Rossby-number regime than single late-type stars 
[
144
, 
145
, 
44
]
.
Accordingly, the fluid motion within this thin H I CZ is expected to be characterized by a low Rossby number, implying a strongly rotationally constrained convection regime 
[
