The reason is the intrinsic rigidity of the universal model: acceleration is provided by universal matter creation, which forces a trade-off between the normalization of the expansion history at intermediate redshift and the amount of acceleration today.
Increasing the matter density can partially restore the intermediate-redshift expansion rate preferred by BAO, but the same change raises the present deceleration parameter, 
